# ============================================================================
#  CSS326 Lab — Test Cases TC01–TC14   (Sourdough Log)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#  Open in VS Code "REST Client" (humao.rest-client) or JetBrains HTTP client.
#  Click "Send Request" above each ### block.
#
#  The rubric is written in library terms (books/loans/members). This file maps
#  each criterion onto THIS app:
#     books/catalog item   -> ingredient   (admin-gated CRUD)
#     borrow / decrement    -> batch creation consumes stock (fires a TRIGGER)
#     stored procedure      -> sp_record_restock / sp_add_batch_with_consumption
#     audit / developer page-> /users  (developer-only)
#
#  COOKIES: the client keeps ONE cookie jar per host. "Logging in" as a role
#  REPLACES the current session, so for the access-control cases just send the
#  right login request immediately before the test. Re-send a login whenever
#  you want to switch role.
#
#  Some criteria (TC01, TC02, TC11) are inspection steps, not HTTP requests.
#  They're written as checklists so this file is a complete test record.
# ============================================================================

@real = http://localhost:3650

# Seeded accounts (sql/seed.sql). Fill in the passwords you seeded with.
@devUser   = dev
@devPass   = dev123
@adminUser = admin
@adminPass = admin123
@userUser  = baker
@userPass  = baker123


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC01 — ERD & schema            [MANUAL / inspection, no request]
#  Expected: 5+ entities, 3+ relationships; a weak-entity FK is in place.
#  Check in MySQL Workbench:
#    Entities: user, starter, feeding, batch, ingredient, stock_movement,
#              consumption_movement, restock_movement  (8)
#    feeding.starter_id      FK -> starter.id   (weak entity: PK = starter_id+feed_time)
#    batch.starter_id        FK -> starter.id
#    batch (starter_id,feeding_time) FK -> feeding
#    stock_movement.ingredient_id FK -> ingredient.id
#  SQL to confirm the FK:
#    SELECT * FROM information_schema.KEY_COLUMN_USAGE
#     WHERE TABLE_NAME='feeding' AND REFERENCED_TABLE_NAME IS NOT NULL;
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC02 — App connects via pool; controller joins   [MANUAL / inspection]
#  Expected: app uses a connection pool; a controller JOINs across tables.
#  Check: .env (DB_HOST/USER/PASS/NAME), config/db.js (mysql2 createPool),
#         controllers/batch.controller.js getAll — JOINs batch + starter.
#  The request below is the live proof that the join works (run TC03-login first):
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████

### TC02 (live) login as admin, then read joined batch list -> rows include starter_name
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{adminUser}}", "password": "{{adminPass}}" }

###
GET {{real}}/batches


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC03 — CRUD Create (Admin)   Expected: 201; row appears in list
#  (run the admin login just above first)
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████

### TC03 create an ingredient -> 201 { id, name, unit, reorder }
# @name createIngredient
POST {{real}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Test Rye Flour", "unit": "g", "reorder": 1000 }

### TC03 verify it is in the list -> find "Test Rye Flour"
GET {{real}}/ingredients


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
