# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC08 — Access control (User)   Expected: server returns 403 on write
#  A normal user must not be able to create/update/delete ingredients.
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████

### TC08a login as USER (baker)
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{userUser}}", "password": "{{userPass}}" }

### TC08b user tries to UPDATE -> 403 "Your role is not allowed to do this"
PUT {{real}}/ingredients/1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Hacked", "unit": "g", "reorder": 0 }

### TC08c user tries to CREATE -> 403
POST {{real}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Sneaky", "unit": "g", "reorder": 1 }

### TC08d user tries to DELETE -> 403
DELETE {{real}}/ingredients/1


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC09 — Access control (Developer)   Expected: developer-only page allowed;
#  Admin and User refused. The developer-only area here is /users.
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████

### TC09a login as DEVELOPER (dev) -> then /users is allowed
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{devUser}}", "password": "{{devPass}}" }

### TC09b developer reads /users -> 200 array of users
GET {{real}}/users

### TC09c now login as ADMIN
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{adminUser}}", "password": "{{adminPass}}" }

### TC09d admin reads /users -> 403 (developer-only)
GET {{real}}/users

### TC09e login as USER, then /users -> 403
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{userUser}}", "password": "{{userPass}}" }

### TC09f user reads /users -> 403
GET {{real}}/users


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC10 — Security: SQL injection on login
#  Expected: login FAILS; no error detail shown. (401, generic message.)
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████

### TC10a classic ' OR '1'='1 in username -> 401
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "' OR '1'='1", "password": "x" }

### TC10b comment-out bypass -> 401
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin' -- ", "password": "x" }

### TC10c always-true + comment -> 401
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "' OR '1'='1' -- ", "password": "x" }

### TC10d inject the password field -> 401
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "' OR '1'='1" }

### TC10e stacked query (table must NOT drop) -> 401
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "'; DROP TABLE user; -- ", "password": "x" }

#  --- extended injection probes on authed inputs (login as any role first) ---

### TC10f :id path param injection -> 400 (validated as integer)
GET {{real}}/starters/%27%20OR%20%271%27=%271

### TC10g query-string filter injection -> 200 empty/filtered, no DB error
GET {{real}}/stock-movements?ingredient_id=%27%20OR%20%271%27=%271

### TC10h BLIND time-based on feeding :feedTime -> INSTANT 400, NOT a 5s wait
#   A ~5s response would mean SLEEP ran (injectable). Fast = safe.
GET {{real}}/feedings/1/2026-01-01%27%20AND%20SLEEP(5)--%20


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC11 — Security: queries use ? placeholders; no creds in code  [MANUAL]
#  Expected: parameterised queries only; credentials live in .env, not source.
#  Check: grep the controllers — every pool.execute uses ? + an array.
#     grep -rn "pool.execute" controllers/      # all use ?, none build SQL by +
#     config/db.js reads process.env.DB_*       # no literal password
#     .env is in .gitignore                      # secrets not committed
#  The only interpolation (batch.controller UPDATE) injects WHITELISTED column
#  names, never user input — values still go through ?.
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC12 — Security: error handling   Expected: generic message to user,
#  detail only in the server log. Trigger a duplicate-key error.
#  (ingredient.name has UNIQUE uq_ingredient_name.)  Login as admin first.
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████

### TC12a login as admin
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{adminUser}}", "password": "{{adminPass}}" }

### TC12b create a name that already exists (run twice if needed) -> 409 generic
#   Response has NO SQL text / stack trace. Raw error is console.error'd server-side.
POST {{real}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Unbleached Bread Flour", "unit": "g", "reorder": 100 }

### TC12c malformed JSON body -> 400 "Bad request" (handled by app.js error mw)
POST {{real}}/ingredients
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "oops", "unit": "g", "reorder": }


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC13 — Trigger   Expected: inserting a 'consumption' stock_movement fires
#  trg_stock_no_negative (BEFORE INSERT on stock_movement). Over-consuming is
#  blocked with SQLSTATE 45000 -> the API returns 409. A valid batch decrements
#  stock. Waste (TC13c-d) and batch create (TC13f-h) both insert consumption
#  rows. Run on a fresh seed.sql so sesame starts at 250 g.
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████

### TC13a login as admin (waste + restock need admin/developer)
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{adminUser}}", "password": "{{adminPass}}" }

### TC13b stock BEFORE -> Toasted Sesame Seeds (id 6) = 250 after a fresh seed
GET {{real}}/ingredients/stock

### TC13c TRIGGER via waste: take 251 g when only 250 g left -> 409 "Not enough in stock..."
#   One gram over is enough: the trigger compares NEW.qty with (restocks - consumptions).
POST {{real}}/stock-movements/waste
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ingredient_id": 6, "qty": 251, "reason": "TC13 trigger test" }

### TC13d boundary: same thing at exactly 1 g -> 201 (trigger lets it through)
POST {{real}}/stock-movements/waste
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ingredient_id": 6, "qty": 1, "reason": "TC13 trigger test" }

### TC13e get a real feeding for starter 1 (TC13f/h read feed_time from this response)
# @name tc13Feedings
GET {{real}}/starters/1/feedings

### TC13f TRIGGER inside the procedure: flour is fine, sesame is too much -> 409 "Not enough stock..."
#   sp_add_batch_with_consumption inserts the batch, then each item. The sesame
#   row fires the SIGNAL, the EXIT HANDLER rolls back -> no batch, no flour row either.
POST {{real}}/batches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "starter_id": 1,
  "feeding_time": "{{tc13Feedings.response.body.$[0].feed_time}}",
  "qty_removed_g": 50,
  "loaf_count": 1,
  "items": [ { "ingredient_id": 1, "qty": 100 }, { "ingredient_id": 6, "qty": 1000 } ]
}

### TC13g proof of rollback: bake list unchanged (still 101 + 102), stock unchanged
GET {{real}}/batches

### TC13h VALID batch within stock -> 201 { id: 104 }  (103 was used up by the rolled-back TC13f: AUTO_INCREMENT is not rolled back)
POST {{real}}/batches
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "starter_id": 1,
  "feeding_time": "{{tc13Feedings.response.body.$[0].feed_time}}",
  "qty_removed_g": 50,
  "loaf_count": 1,
  "items": [ { "ingredient_id": 1, "qty": 100 }, { "ingredient_id": 6, "qty": 100 } ]
}

### TC13i stock AFTER -> sesame 250 - 1 - 100 = 149, flour down 100
GET {{real}}/ingredients/stock


# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████
#  TC14 — Stored procedure   Expected: an SP runs via an endpoint.
#  restock calls sp_record_restock; batch create calls
#  sp_add_batch_with_consumption (TC13). Restock needs admin/developer.
# ████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████████

### TC14a login as admin
POST {{real}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "{{adminUser}}", "password": "{{adminPass}}" }

### TC14b call sp_record_restock via the endpoint -> 201 { ingredient_id, qty, cost }
POST {{real}}/stock-movements/restock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "ingredient_id": 1, "qty": 5000, "cost": 175 }

### TC14c confirm the SP wrote a 'restock' stock_movement row
GET {{real}}/stock-movements?ingredient_id=1